.TH READLINK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
readlink \- read a symbolic link target
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t readlink(const char* " path ", char* " buffer ", size_t " byte_count ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B readlink
copies up to
.I byte_count
bytes from the symbolic link target to the writable buffer. It does not append
a NUL terminator. A result equal to the buffer size may indicate truncation.
The caller must supply enough writable storage for the count.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes copied on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.B errno .
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lstat (3crunch),
.BR readlink (2)
